shape theory.coherence.law3 : theory.coherence, theory.contact.self, theory.contact.incompatibility {
  type: law
  layer: 0
  """
// Law 3 (Consistency).
// In a coherent shape, coupled incompatible shapes must resolve
// or trigger dissolution.
//
// A shape whose internal character contains contradictory demands
// on its own structure cannot produce a well-defined transformation:
// S cannot simultaneously satisfy incompatible requirements. Either
// the contradiction resolves (through transformation that eliminates
// the incompatibility) or the shape dissolves.
//
// Self-contact requires internal consistency.
//
// Extension to mutual contact: if A and B are incompatible and in
// contact, A's structure cannot produce coherent output from
// incompatible character. Either the incompatibility resolves or
// incoherence propagates.
//
// Derives from: theory.coherence, theory.contact.self,
//               theory.contact.incompatibility
  """
}
